row(26, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'THE REUBENITE — THE FIRST SUMMARY, THE FIRST COUNT: 43,730 AGAINST 46,500; THE ONE COUNT NOT A ROUND HUNDRED. "{H(26, 7, "אלה", "משפחת", "הראובני", "ויהיו", "פקדיהם")}" ("these are the families of THE REUBENITE, and their counted ones were" — the summary in the tribe-gentilic form (Reubenite, Simeonite, Zebulunite, and Dan\'s Shuhamite; the other eight say "the sons of" or the bare name); "and their counted ones were" here and at the Levites (26:62) alone — the other summaries say "by their counted ones" or "and their counted ones" (computed)) "{H(26, 7, "שלשה", "וארבעים", "אלף", "ושבע", "מאות", "ושלשים")}" ("three and forty thousand and seven hundred and thirty" — {cnt(7, "Reuben")}; 43,730 is the ONE count of this census not a round hundred, as Gad\'s 45,650 was the one of the first; computed) → {A(26, 7, "אלין", "זרעית", "ראובן", "והוו", "מניניהון")} ("these are the seed-groups of Reuben, and their counts were") {A(26, 7, "ארבעין", "ותלתא", "אלפין", "ושבע", "מאה", "ותלתין")} ("FORTY AND THREE thousand and seven hundred and thirty" — the translation reverses the ink\'s "three and forty", cut from the shelf\'s bytes). The register: "and they were".')
