row(26, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'THE EARTH OPENED ITS MOUTH — 16:32\'S CLAUSE, TWO SEATS; AND KORACH — NAMED AMONG THE SWALLOWED AND SET AT THE FIRE; THEY BECAME A SIGN — THE SERPENT\'S POLE-WORD. "{H(26, 10, "ותפתח", "הארץ", "את", "פיה", "ותבלע", "אתם")}" ("and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them" — 16:32\'s clause word for word, the two seats alone in the Bible (Deuteronomy 11:6 says "the earth gaped", Psalm 106:17 "the earth opened and swallowed Dathan"); computed) "{H(26, 10, "ואת", "קרח", "במות", "העדה", "באכל", "האש", "את", "חמשים", "ומאתים", "איש")}" ("AND KORACH, in the death of the company, when the fire consumed the two hundred and fifty men" — sitting 5 found Korach UNNAMED among the swallowed at 16:32 ("them and their houses and every man of Korach\'s"); here the roster names him with the swallowed AND sets him "in the death of the company when the fire consumed" — one verse, both deaths: the ink\'s evidence for the tape\'s open checkpoint CK4 (Korach\'s death-mode) and the exam\'s Sanhedrin 110a (burned, swallowed, or neither); the parser reads 250 — 16:35\'s number; computed) "{H(26, 10, "ויהיו", "לנס")}" ("and they became A SIGN" — the noun\'s Torah four: "the LORD is my BANNER" (Exodus 17:15), the serpent\'s POLE (21:8, 9) and this — the other tokens of the letters are the verb "flee" (35:6, 25; Deuteronomy 4:42) and "abated" (34:7); 17:3\'s "a sign" for the censers was another word (ot); the rebels\' fate the pole-word of the healing serpent; computed) → {A(26, 10, "ופתחת", "ארעא", "ית", "פומה", "ובלעת", "יתהון", "וית", "קרח", "במותא", "דכנשתא")} ("and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them and Korach in the death of the congregation"); {A(26, 10, "והוו", "לאת")} ("and they became a SIGN" — the pole-word rendered by the sign-word, cut from the shelf\'s bytes). The register: "and it opened", "and it swallowed", "and they were".')
row(26, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'BUT THE SONS OF KORACH DID NOT DIE — THE ROSTER\'S ONE EXCEPTION, ELEVEN PSALMS\' HEADING. "{H(26, 11, "ובני", "קרח", "לא", "מתו")}" ("and the sons of Korach DID NOT DIE" — a four-word verse, one seat; "did not die" elsewhere only of the men of Ashdod (1 Samuel 5:12); the sons\' line runs to the singers — "for the sons of Korach" heads ELEVEN psalms (42, 44-49, 84, 85, 87, 88) and Samuel descends from Korah (1 Chronicles 6); the family "of Korah" stands in the Levite roster below (26:58) where Izhar\'s does not — the line that did not die named for the grandson; computed) → {A(26, 11, "ובני", "קרח", "לא", "מיתו")} ("and the sons of Korach did not die"). No narrative verb (the perfect).')
